            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0610" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg494"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857 T53/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul General at
                            Halifax to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax, Nova Scotia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mackay-Bennett cable that boat is due Halifax Thursday with bodies recovered from
                    wreck of the <hi rendition="#italic">Titanic</hi>. Are there any penalties
                    necessary preparatory to shipping bodies across border to New York?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ragsdale.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
